Subject: [PATCH 5/5] LAB: classify decrypted requests into child applications;
 pd block on TUNNEL_CLOSED (PRO-504)

Inspected tunnels see each inner HTTP request in clear, which is where the
detector's child applications (go/detector AppClassifier, protocol-detector
PR #163) can be told apart: gmail-uploading inside gmail. Visibility only:
the verdict is computed before the exchange and never passed to it.

- internal/pdobs: the closed vocabularies (basis, reason, limit) and the
  application-name shape check; anything else is logged as "unknown".
- internal/protodetect: a Culvert-owned AppClassifier interface; real_apps.go
  is the only file naming the library API. A test keeps pdobs equal to the
  library's vocabularies.
- childapp_lab.go: CULVERT_LAB_CHILDAPP=real turns it on (default off: nil
  tally, no entry, zero added allocations). The H1 loop and each H2 stream
  note their request (H2 before the reshape clears RequestURI); at tunnel end
  a log-only TUNNEL_CLOSED entry carries the nested "pd" block: requests,
  at most 8 distinct verdicts with counts, apps_dropped, releases. It holds
  no host, path or header value; the entry's host is redacted at
  persistLogEntry like every other entry, and the rule's log-traffic flag
  gates it.
- logstore.Entry gains PD (block-level omitempty: absent when off).

Local lab only; never proposed upstream.
